<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Track</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Ranger (guild level 6)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>track &lt;player or monster&gt;
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>track deer
</pre>
<p>You study the ground for your quarry's tracks and learn which way they 
went: "You search and see some tracks to the north." Follow them a room 
at a time, and track again. You may also find that the tracks lead to 
this very place, or into something here, such as a ship or a cart. Your 
quarry can be anywhere in the world, though tracks close by are the 
easiest to find.
</p><p>Your skill decides whether you can read the tracks, with your brain and 
level against your quarry's. Each try costs endurance, more in cities, 
indoors and on ice than in the open. You must be standing, and you can't 
track on water.
</p><p>To follow the tracks without stopping, and attack when you find your 
quarry, use <a cmd='#'>Help Hunt</a>.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Hunt</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Locate</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Ranger Skills</a>
</pre>




</div>